es throughout the planet. As Continental states occupied fresh countries, those conveyed along with those their individual societies, tongues, and practices of lifestyle, regularly obliging indigenous groups to incorporate or encounter exclusion. Autochthonous peoples forfeited their domains, intrinsic supplies, and freedom since their regions were seized for colonial expansion. They also suffered from violence, exploitation, and the spread of diseases brought by the colonizers. Today, the effects of colonialism continue to be felt, as indigenous communities struggle to preserve their cultural heritage, regain their land rights, and overcome the socio-economic disparities that were perpetuated by colonial rule.", "encoding_time_report": {"container_generation": 3.75, "secret_key_generation": 93.1}, "decoding_time": 0.0003209114074707031, "decoded_message": "0110011010010110001101001111000101011101010110100100010111011010", "error_message": ""}